{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>In the thickness of the cloud</b> — this is the ערפל (thick darkness) where Elohim was (Exodus 20:21), and all saw and recognized it to be so, as it says: \"and the appearance of the glory of YHWH was like a devouring fire on the top of the mountain before the eyes of the children of Israel\" (Exodus 24:17)." "<b>So that the people will hear when I speak with you</b>. Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said that there were among Israel people whose prophecy was in doubt, and even though it is written (Exodus 14:31) \"and they believed in YHWH and in Moses His servant,\" there it says \"and Israel saw,\" and not all Israel, and this is what they said to him: \"this day we have seen that Elohim will speak with man and he lives\" (Deuteronomy 5:21), for they did not believe so at first. And this is the meaning of <b>so that the people will hear when I speak with you</b> — the Ten Commandments — <b>and also in you they will believe</b>, that you are a prophet, for from now on the matter of prophecy will be verified among them. But this is not correct, for the seed of Abraham would not be in doubt about prophecy, for they believed in it from their forefathers. And Scripture already said further: \"and the people believed and heard\" (Exodus 4:31), \"and they believed in YHWH and in Moses His servant\" (Exodus 14:31), and if it did not say there \"all the people\" and \"all Israel,\" here too it was not said \"so that all the people will hear\".<br>And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that He said: I <b>come to you in the thickness of the cloud</b>, so that you will approach the ערפל (thick darkness) <b>in order that the people will hear My words</b>, and they themselves will be prophets through My words — not that they should believe from the mouth of others, as it says: \"when YHWH said to me: assemble Me the people and I will make them hear My words, that they may learn to fear Me all the days\" (Deuteronomy 4:10) — <b>and also in you they will believe</b> forever, throughout all the generations. And if a prophet or a dreamer of dreams arises among them to contradict your word, they will deny him immediately, for they have already seen with their own eyes and heard with their own ears that you attained the supreme level of prophecy. From you it will be clarified for them what is written (Numbers 12:6–8): \"if there be a prophet among you, YHWH, in a vision I make Myself known to him, in a dream I speak with him; not so My servant Moses, in all My house he is trusted — mouth to mouth I speak with him.\" Therefore He said <b>so that the people will hear when I speak with you</b>, for they will hear My words from within the fire and will know that I am YHWH speaking with you, and they will believe in My words, <b>and also in you forever</b>. And likewise what they said — \"this day we have seen that Elohim will speak with man and he lives\" (Deuteronomy 5:21) — is to say: behold, the matter has been fulfilled among us by the sight of our own eyes as was the desire of Elohim, and from now on <b>you draw near</b>, so that we may know of you that you attained the supreme greatness, <b>and hear all that YHWH will say</b>, and we will hear from your mouth and do, for your prophecy is already verified, for it is the highest above all the prophets.<br>And in the Mekhilta (here) I found: <b>so that the people will hear when I speak with you</b> — this teaches that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: behold, I call you from the top of the mountain and you ascend, as it says (Exodus 19:20) \"and YHWH called Moses,\" <b>and also in you they will believe forever</b> — both in you and in the prophets who are destined to arise after you. Their words accord with the opinion of Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:11:01.878027250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}